/// so the NaN that survives is `b.y`, then `a.y`, then the y term. Writing the
/// expression as `b.y * a.y + a.x * b.x` reproduces exactly that, keeping the
/// result bit-identical to the C for NaN inputs too.
#[unsafe(no_mangle)]
pub extern "C" fn c2Dot(a: c2v, b: c2v) -> f32 {
    b.y * a.y + a.x * b.x
}"""
