[38;5;252m[1m## Three real bugs found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m1. [38;5;10mc2Clip[0m aborted the process where C returns 3.[22m When both endpoint distances are negative, [38;5;10msp == 2[0m; if [38;5;10md0 * d1[0m then [3munderflows to [38;5;10m+0.0[0m[23m, the [38;5;10md0 * d1 <= 0[0m branch also fires and C executes [38;5;10mout[sp++][0m with [38;5;10msp == 2[0m. Disassembly showed C's [38;5;10mout[0m at [38;5;10m-0x30(%rbp)[0m and the already-dead [38;5;10mfloat d1[0m at [38;5;10m-0x1c(%rbp)[0m, so the stray 8-byte store lands harmlessly on [38;5;10md1[0m and the only observable effect is a return value of [38;5;10m3[0m. The Rust used a checked index into a 2-element array, so with [38;5;10mpanic = "abort"[0m it killed the process. Fixed with a third write-only scratch slot.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m2. [38;5;10mc2GJK[0m bounds-checked the caller's cache indices.[22m [38;5;10mcache->iA[0m/[38;5;10miB[0m are entirely unvalidated by C, but the Rust indexed [38;5;10mpA.verts[iA as usize][0m on a [38;5;10m[c2v; 8][0m — any index outside [38;5;10m0..8[0m aborted. Replaced with unchecked pointer arithmetic.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m3. [38;5;10mc2AABBtoCapsuleManifold[0m read the wrong bytes for [38;5;10mp->verts[-1][0m.[22m With a non-finite AABB every [38;5;10mc2Norms[0m normal is NaN, so [38;5;10mindex[0m keeps its initial [38;5;10m~0 == -1[0m and C evaluates [38;5;10mverts[-1][0m — which, since [38;5;10mverts[0m sits at offset 4 of [38;5;10mc2Poly[0m, reads 4 bytes [3mbefore[23m the struct. C's [38;5;10m-O0[0m frame puts [38;5;10mc2Poly p[0m at [38;5;10m-0xa0(%rbp)[0m and the spilled [38;5;10mc2AABB A[0m at [38;5;10m-0xb0[0m, so C deterministically reads [38;5;10m(A.max.y, bitcast(4))[0m. Reproduced with a [38;5;10m#[repr(C)][0m wrapper whose leading field is [38;5;10mA.max.y[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Two limits I could not remove, and why[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mc2MakeProxy[0m has no [38;5;10mC2_TYPE_POLY[0m case, yet [38;5;10mc2CapsuletoPolyManifold[0m calls [38;5;10mc2GJK[0m with [38;5;10mC2_TYPE_POLY[0m — so C [1mreads an uninitialized [38;5;10mc2Proxy[0m[22m on the live [38;5;10momni_manifold(AABB, CAPSULE)[0m path. I confirmed with a standalone C driver that the C returns the all-zero-proxy answer on a zeroed stack and garbage (or segfaults in [38;5;10mc2Support[0m) on a dirty one. No Rust implementation can match arbitrary call histories; zero-init is the only reproducible choice, so the tests zero the stack before every call, and [38;5;10mrow64_non_finite_inputs[0m requires the C's own two entry points to disagree before tolerating anything.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Separately, x86 [38;5;10maddss[0m/[38;5;10mmulss[0m return the [3mdestination[23m operand on NaN, and gcc [38;5;10m-O0[0m vs LLVM [38;5;10m-O3[0m pick different destinations for [38;5;10mc2Dot[0m's final add. Reordering the Rust source does not help — LLVM canonicalizes commutative [38;5;10mfadd[0m (verified by disassembly). So a NaN [3mresult[23m may carry a different sign bit when the caller supplies two differently-payloaded NaNs. Everything else is bit-identical, including [38;5;10m±inf[0m, [38;5;10m±0.0[0m, subnormals, and all internally generated NaNs. Tests use strict bit equality everywhere except NaN-input paths, which use [38;5;10mfeq_nan[0m (strict unless [3mboth[23m values are NaN).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Both are written up in [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m with the measurements behind them.[0m[0m
